8127                 		.TITLE	Command Names Table
8128                 	
8129                 	
8130                 	;   This table gives the names of all the commands known to the monitor.  Each
8131                 	; entry consists of a one or two letter command name, in SIXBIT, followed by
8132                 	; the address of a routine to execute it.  Although this table is stored in
8133                 	; field 1, all the command routines are implicitly in field zero!  The zero
8134                 	; entry at the end is a "catch all" that is called if none of the previous
8135                 	; names match, and points to an error routine.  With the exception of this last
8136                 	; entry, the order of the table is not significant.
